  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support strategic dialogue &quot;Future Resilience from mountain to coast&quot; (for Northern Java)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implemented from November 2023 to September 2024, this project aimed to advance strategic dialogue that contributes to designing a multi-year programme on Integrated Water Resilience under the Memorandum of Understanding on Water (MoU Water) between the governments of Indonesia and the Netherlands. The project facilitated a structured process to identify shared ambitions, thematic interests and collaboration areas of mutual benefit. Through consultations with a joint core team of Indonesian and Dutch stakeholders, one-on-one engagements and multi-stakeholder dialogues, the project outlined major components for future cooperation including nature-based solutions, urban water resilience, water governance and participation. It also mapped initial steps and a workplan to guide further dialogue towards the next Joint Steering Committee (JSC) session, helping establish a clear roadmap for continued engagement beyond the project&#x2019;s completion. By providing a forum for joint reflection and planning, the project supported enhanced mutual understanding and alignment of priorities between both governments. It laid the groundwork for a resilient, programmatic bilateral partnership on integrated water management and climate adaptation in Indonesia&#x2019;s northern Java region.</narrative>
  </description>
